      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Endoscopic ultrasound (EUS)-guided ethanol ablation has emerged as an efficacious and safe alternative management option for pancreatic cysts. We undertook a meta-analysis and systematic review to assess the overall safety and efficacy of EUS-guided ethanol ablation of pancreatic cysts."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "METHOD STUDY SELECTION CRITERIA",
          "content": "EUS-guided ethanol ablation of pancreatic cysts."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "DATA COLLECTION EXTRACTION",
          "content": "Articles were searched in Medline, Pubmed, and Ovid journals."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STATISTICAL METHOD",
          "content": "Fixed and random effects models were used to calculate the pooled proportions."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Initial search identified 1,319 reference articles, in which 120 relevant articles were selected and reviewed. Data was extracted from seven studies (n\u2009=\u2009152) of EUS-guided ethanol ablation of pancreatic cysts, which met the inclusion criteria. With EUS-guided ethanol ablation, the pooled proportion of patients with complete cyst resolution was 56.20 % (95 % CI\u2009=\u200948.16 to 64.08) and partial cyst resolution was 23.72 % (95 % CI\u2009=\u200917.24 to 30.89). Postprocedural complications after ablation were significant for abdominal pain in 6.51 % (95 % CI\u2009=\u20093.12 to 11.04) and pancreatitis in 3.90 % (95 % CI\u2009=\u20091.39 to 7.60) of the pooled percentage of patients. Publication bias calculated using Harbord-Egger bias indicator gave a value of -1.09 (95 % CI\u2009=\u200910.21 to 8.03, p\u2009=\u20090.77). The Begg-Mazumdar indicator gave a Kendall's tau b value of 0.05 (p\u2009≥\u20090.99)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "EUS-guided ethanol ablation may be a safe alternative treatment modality for pancreatic cysts, with acceptable intraprocedural and postprocedural complications. However, due to the limited data available, prospective randomized controlled trials with a long follow up period are required in this area."
        }
      ]},
